module gunbc.rung_drop.v1_required_lanes_withdrawn

import std.types { List, NonEmptyStr, String }
import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, Enumerated, ReplacementStaged }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// DECLARED 2026-10-09 ON AN OPERATOR RULING (the brief to session smart-gull-336, the v2 half of the
// v1 withdrawal): "v1 is effectively bankrupt due to memory instability - i want to go back to pure
// v2 native compiler development - that means deleting most of our current CI jobs", and "i suggest
// we bankrupt the current CI first". The change that carries this row deletes four of the five lanes
// the required context read -- `floor`, `generated`, `rust-unit-tests` and `seed` -- from
// gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow and leaves the emit-and-build steps as the one required job,
// `witnesses` (the same ruling collapsed `emit-build` and the aggregate that read it into that job,
// and requires it to emit and build both products fresh on every run).
//
// WHY THE LANES ARE DELETED AND NOT GIVEN HEADROOM. The floor already ran at its slot's throttle
// line (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode required_floor_runs_at_its_memory_ceiling carries that receipt),
// and every repair on offer -- a larger slot, an allocator setting, a narrower subject -- spends work
// on the interpreter the ruling retires. The ruling withdraws v1 as a validation authority; it does
// not ask for a cheaper v1 gate.
//
// THIS IS A DROP AND NOT A CLEAN-UP, WHICH IS WHY IT IS ONE ROW WITH A WIDE POPULATION. Nothing the
// four lanes held is held by anything else today. The surviving job establishes that the seed emits
// two v2 closures and that the emitted crates build and start, and a green required context says
// that and nothing more.
//
// AMENDED 2026-10-11 ON AN OPERATOR REQUEST ("could you make the regeneration CI step and we can see?"),
// narrowed to the files whose drift breaks a build: a NON-REQUIRED regeneration and push-back exists.
// `gunbc.heal_workflow` runs on same-repository pull requests that touch the generation inputs (its
// trigger paths derive from `witness_layer_roots`, `src/v1/**` and `gunbc.seed_build_artifact_emit`
// `seed_build_artifacts`), converges the stage0 mirrors with `claim_executor --regen-round-cost` to
// first_generation_equal, writes the eleven seed-build artifacts without loading the registry
// (`gunbc.instruments.seed_build_artifacts_regen`), and seals the changed files as a candidate;
// `gunbc.heal_publisher_workflow` re-derives it from the default branch and pushes ONE bot commit,
// compare-and-set on the head sha, never forced, with a receipt comment naming each artifact. A fork
// pull request gets a visible notice, not a repair. IT JUDGES NOTHING AND IS NOT A REQUIRED CONTEXT: a
// regeneration that refuses (the round did not converge) pushes nothing, and a green or absent heal run
// says nothing about the population above. It narrows members (3) and (4) of the trigger for the
// stage0 mirrors and the seed-build artifacts only, as a REPAIR; the registry-wide artifacts
// (workflows, documents, product artifacts) are still compared by nothing on a pull request.
//
// WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT DO. It does not amend the rows that already described losses on these lanes
// (required_gate_bankruptcy, witness_floor_off_the_required_gate,
// required_lanes_do_not_resolve_product_layer_modules, v1_integration_tests_deleted_from_the_unit_lane
// and their neighbours). Their triggers name capabilities, and a native lane can still fire them. The
// one row this change does supersede is rust_unit_tests_off_pull_requests, whose own text says the
// unit lane still blocks at the merge queue; it no longer runs anywhere.

data v1_required_lanes_withdrawn_population: FreeSemigroup<String> = FreeSemigroup { head: "every claim the `floor` lane folded on a pull request or a merge_group: the prepared subject of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` with its seeds, plus the changed-witness and touched-entry selection. `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane witnesses` is run by no job. THE WET CLAIM LANE IS ENUMERATED BY IDENTITY, NOT BY PROSE: every claim enrolled in `v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal` `local_repo_wet_schedule` (all ExpectedToHold) was executed only by this lane, and is executed by no required job.", tail: ["the stage0 mirrors equal one emission by the seed built from them, and the registry-rostered generated artifacts (`gunbc.generated_artifact_registry` `committed_generated_artifacts`) equal one emission of their authorities: `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane build` is run by no job. That population includes `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` and `DESIGN.md`, so the gate's own workflow file is compared with `gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow` by nothing; the heal publisher workflow that published repair candidates was deleted with the lanes and is restored by the amendment below (`gunbc.heal_publisher_workflow`, publishing under the WIF pool of `gunbc.auth.heal_publisher_federation`)", "the position of each registered `.dag` generated artifact: the `gunbc.generated_artifact_registry` rows whose `artifact_path` ends `.dag` (the predicate is the population; at the source layout cutover they are `dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_crate_layout_generated.dag`, `dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_crate_partition_generated.dag` and `dag/gunbc/stage0/stage0_executable_assembly_generated.dag`). No required compile reaches any of them -- each is outside the import closures of `gunbc.instrument_targets` `self_host_entry` and `v2_native_cli_entry` -- so a required step refuses a registered file that exists at a position other than the rule position of its module line (the layout check, `v2.compiler.source_authority` `layout_check`), and nothing on the required path refuses a registered file that is absent, or a registry row moved away from its producer. The layout check deliberately reads no registry (single authority: whether a file is generated is the registry's fact, and the registry's import closure is far larger than the compiler's own CLI). The mitigation is the claim `v2.test.claim.generated_dag_artifacts_at_rule_position`, which observes each registered `.dag` artifact once (`gunbc.generated_artifact_observation` `observe_generated_artifact_with`) and refuses one that is absent, unobservable, unequal to what its real producer emits, or whose module line is not the rule position of its registered path; it is executed when the claim set is run and is not run on `witnesses`", "the lint: `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (`gunbc.repo.repo_self_build` `repo_self_clippy_command`), the only command that compiles the integration-test and example targets", "the v1 unit tests: `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib` (`gunbc.repo.repo_self_build` `repo_self_test_command`), which ran on merge_group and workflow_dispatch", "module resolution: every module the source-root ingestion admits under dag/ and src/v2/ that is outside the import closures of `gunbc.instrument_targets` `self_host_entry` and `v2_native_cli_entry` is handed to a compiler by no required step, so it can stop resolving on main with the required context green. Enumerated BY IDENTITY, not by count, by `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:required-lane-resolution-census` (`gunbc.required_lane_resolution_census_live`), which from this change does not hold by design", "the consumers of those lanes' products: no merge_group run uploads a compiler pair candidate. Fleet-desired admission, which used to build that pair and advance `refs/fleet/desired`, is withdrawn: the admitted revision is what has landed on `origin/main`. `gunbc.fleet.fleet_revision_acceptance` still names a required-CI success that carries the `witnesses` job's emit-and-build verdict, under the contract epoch `gunbc.required_ci_contract_epoch` moved to with the lane withdrawal, and is not the production admission path", "the regeneration of what `gunbc.heal_workflow` does not cover is owed by the author: the registry-rostered artifacts other than the stage0 mirrors and the eleven seed-build artifacts; `gunbc.drift_watch_workflow` only reports drift of the workflows, runner sudoers, githooks, `.gitignore`, `.gitattributes` and fci1 context on a schedule and repairs none, and the merge driver, plans, doc projections and product artifacts are compared by nothing. The push-back job repairs and never refuses a merge, so a stage0 mirror or seed-build artifact it did not repair (a fork pull request, a non-converging round, a moved head) is compared by nothing", "NOT ENUMERATED HERE, and named so the gap is not read as empty: every `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` row and every standing `gunbc.rung_drop` row whose stated current rung is held by a step of the four lanes. Those rows are not amended by this change, and each now sits no higher than this row's temporary rung", "THE AUTHORED REQUIRED-FLOOR ROSTER IS ENUMERATED BY IDENTITY, NOT BY PROSE: every row of `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_authored_modules` -- the seeded subject list of the deleted manual required-floor runner (`src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/required_floor_runner.rs`, no caller; the floor lane of this very withdrawal was its last executor, and the closing-contract witness that reads the roster runs nowhere either) -- is a member of this population by module identity: it resolves under the source-root ingestion, and no required lane's compile closure reaches it today, so no required job can execute it (reaching a closure is resolution, not execution: the census reads resolution grain only). The population is re-derived, one `roster` receipt line per row tagged with its standing, by `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:required-lane-resolution-census` (`gunbc.required_lane_resolution_census_live`, which reads the roster as DATA so an added row is enumerated without amending this text, and REFUSES -- exit 2, naming the row -- if a roster row names no `.dag` module, , and NARROWED 2026-11-01 on its last member: the required job now COMPILES the v1 unit-test harness without running it -- `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib --no-run`, spelled once in `gunbc.repo.repo_self_build` `repo_self_test_compile_command` and carried by `gunbc.witness.compiler_gate_workflow` `compiler_gate_v1_unit_test_compile_step`, controlled by `test.claim.compiler_gate_emit_build_lane_witness` `the_v1_unit_test_harness_is_compiled_on_the_required_job`. What this row holds withdrawn is the EXECUTION of that population, and execution stays withdrawn: `--no-run` links the harness and runs no test body, the member's restoration trigger is unmet, and a compile is not a verdict"] }

data v1_required_lanes_withdrawn: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "v1_required_lanes_withdrawn" as NonEmptyStr,
  subject: "The four v1-judged required lanes (`floor`, `generated`, `rust-unit-tests`, `seed`) as a merge gate",
  declared: "2026-10-09",
  standing: Standing { declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: ReplacementStaged {
      replacement: "a binary built from an emission of v2 judging this population on the required path, admitted to the gate as rows of `gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate` `emitted_subject_build_rows`. No such row covers any member of this population at declaration"
    },
    population: Enumerated { members: v1_required_lanes_withdrawn_population },
    restoration_trigger: "THE CAPABILITY: on every landing revision, a binary built from an emission of v2 -- the seed's emission today, v2's own after the generation transition -- judges this population on the required path with a discriminating red. Member by member: (1) every claim the floor folded is executed by such a binary, or its subject has been deleted; (2) every module the source-root ingestion admits is resolved, observed as `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:required-lane-resolution-census` holding against the workflow as emitted, WITHIN the required slot's memory_max (gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired gunbc_runner_slot_memory_max_bytes) -- MEASURED BLOCKER: `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:native-process-memory-census` reports the native census over the whole corpus peaking above that slot, and the unreached population is nearly the whole corpus, so a subset or a closure shard neither fits nor avoids re-paying shared closures; the capability restored is that the native compiler judges the population within the slot's memory_max; (3) every committed generated artifact, `.github/workflows/witnesses.yml` included, is compared with one emission of its authority; (1a) the native binary executes the `local_repo_wet_schedule` claims on a required job with their host effects bounded; (4) for the three members whose subject is v1's own Rust -- the stage0 mirrors, the lint and the v1 unit tests -- a change to the seed's sources cannot land with the required context green unless a required step judged it, or the seed no longer exists. WHAT THAT MUST BE SUFFICIENT FOR: no member of this population can regress with the required context green. NARROWEST CAPABILITY FOR THE RECURRING-FAILURE-MODE LEDGER: the emitted compiler infers the std/extdeps closure of the ledger rows (inferred approaches modules) so record-literal field completeness is judged per row and a rung-less row is a located file_refusal. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THIS ROW, stated because each is the likely mistake: returning any of the four lanes, or any step that hands the corpus to the v1 interpreter, because the ruling withdraws that authority; a native row that judges part of the population, which narrows this row member by member and retires nothing; a manual or dispatched run off the required path; and a count of claims or modules standing where the identity join belongs. The TEMPORARY rung is Mitigatable only while the seed's own runners for these members exist at head, so a change that deletes one of them owes its own declaration."
  } }
}
